---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import StateLots from '../../components/StateLots.astro';
import { href } from '../../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, faqNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../../lib/schema';

const title = 'Can a Nevada HOA ban RV parking? | RV Storage Prices';
const description =
  'NRS 116.350 is quoted from the Nevada Legislature. It allows reasonable restrictions on recreational vehicles and watercraft. Not legal advice.';
const path = '/guides/can-hoa-ban-rv-parking-nevada/';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'Guides', path: '/guides/' },
  { label: 'Nevada HOA parking', path },
];
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Can a Nevada HOA ban RV parking?',
    a: 'NRS 116.350 subsection 2 says an association may adopt rules that reasonably restrict the parking or storage of recreational vehicles, watercraft, trailers, or commercial vehicles, to the extent authorized by law. It is not a right to keep one in a driveway.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does that section cover a public road?',
    a: 'Subsection 1 limits regulation of a public road in a community that is not gated and whose access is not controlled. The RV sentence is subsection 2. Read both on the Nevada rules page.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where is RV storage in Nevada if the house does not allow it?',
    a: 'The city list on this page links the Nevada storage lots in this directory. A listing is not permission to park at the house.',
  },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: '2026-11-20' }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
  faqNode(faqs),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Can a Nevada HOA ban RV parking?</h1>
    <p>
      This is not legal advice and not a reading of your governing documents. The longer note is the
      <a href={href('/rules/nevada/')}>Nevada HOA rules page</a>. Checked November 19, 2026, on the
      <a href="https://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-116.html" rel="noopener noreferrer">Nevada Legislature’s copy of NRS Chapter 116</a>.
    </p>
    <p>NRS 116.350 subsection 2 says:</p>
    <blockquote>
      <p>
        Except as otherwise provided in subsection 3, the provisions of subsection 1 do not preclude an
        association from adopting, and do not preclude the governing documents of an association from
        setting forth, rules that reasonably restrict the parking or storage of recreational vehicles,
        watercraft, trailers or commercial vehicles in the common-interest community to the extent
        authorized by law. The governing documents of an association may authorize the executive board
        of the association to impose a fine pursuant to NRS 116.31031 for any violation of the rules
        authorized pursuant to this subsection.
      </p>
    </blockquote>
    <p>
      That sentence allows reasonable restrictions. It is not a right to keep a recreational vehicle or
      a boat on a driveway.
    </p>
    <StateLots stateSlug="nevada" inputId="hoa-nv" />
    <section class="faq">
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <>
          <h3>{faq.q}</h3>
          <p>{faq.a}</p>
        </>
      ))}
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
